wirecap: the hub gains a sink (Hub::setSink)

A sink sees every packet published on an enabled channel, on the publisher's thread, before the
packet is queued and whether or not it is, with the time exactly as the caller passed it (0 when it
passed none). With files, live and gsmtap off the hub opens no file and no socket, so a program can
take the packets straight from the decoders. onair-rx's build.sh applies this patch to the copy of
the OnAir checkout it builds from.

---
